http://news.albasani.net/

That site runs a pretty full featured News service
with a good assortment of newsgroups.

It requires you to establish a (free) account and
login after receiving a confirmation email; this
process can take a day or two.

It limits you to 25 postings a day but as much
reading as you like, so far as I can tell.

The site is pretty good about filtering spam.

I access it through the mail/News interface built
into SeaMonkey. It works smoothly there, allowing
me to read threads or articles by arrival time,
either forward in time or backward in time.

Probably any combined mail/NNTP-News client would
work fairly well, Microsoft ones least so.

For me, it's a nice backup for when Google Groups
temporarily throttles my postings, or otherwise
goes temporarily insane.

